WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.000
The private ShelfLife plugin offers expiry, stock and pick
previews. The recording uses an owned development store.

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:10.000
Shopify confirms the development store approved read access.

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:13.000
Choose Continue to ChatGPT to finish connecting.

00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:17.000
The connected-store tool succeeds. The response identifies
a live ShelfLife connection.

00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:20.000
The changesStock field is false.

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:26.000
The user asks which lots need attention in the next 14 days
and requests that stock stay unchanged.

00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:30.000
The expiry brief found no expired or upcoming lots
from October 8 through October 22.

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:34.000
It returned zero units at expiry risk and zero lots
with missing expiry dates.

00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:38.000
The batch search returned The Complete Snowboard, Dawn,
with an expiry date of January 31, 2027.

00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:41.000
The result contained two units, with zero on hold.

00:00:41.000 --> 00:00:45.000
The variant stock report found one batch and two pickable units.

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:48.000
Both units had an unknown cost, so no monetary value was reported.

00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:55.000
The batch history returned zero recorded movements.
The history covers stock operations recorded in ShelfLife.

00:00:55.000 --> 00:00:59.000
A three-unit pick preview allocated the two available units
at the requested location.

00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:03.000
The shortage was one unit. The preview returned
changesStock false, and stock stayed unchanged.

00:01:03.000 --> 00:01:07.000
ShelfLife settings show the approved ChatGPT connection
and a Disconnect control.

00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:10.000
Disconnecting ends future reads. This recorded connection
remained active at the end of the demonstration.
